00:10:49.325 --> 00:10:54.995
Going back to that, well, that just
means that we have two chiral, so we

00:10:54.995 --> 00:10:59.984
have achiral molecules, sorry, and they
are mirrors, however, they are achiral.

00:11:01.114 --> 00:11:02.714
Let's take a look at the next example.

00:11:03.035 --> 00:11:07.175
Okay, our first example, are the
following molecules enantiomers

00:11:07.214 --> 00:11:09.054
or are they the same molecule?

00:11:09.725 --> 00:11:14.835
Now, in order for them to be enantiomers,
Or the same, what does that exactly mean?

00:11:14.875 --> 00:11:17.145
Well, same just tells
you they're identical.

00:11:17.215 --> 00:11:20.845
Not that they are achiral or
chiral, just that they're identical.

00:11:21.395 --> 00:11:23.814
So in order to first, we need
to determine are they chiral?

00:11:24.255 --> 00:11:27.665
Well, if I go through these, I
can try to always highlight that I

00:11:27.675 --> 00:11:30.325
have four completely unique groups.

00:11:30.754 --> 00:11:33.135
So we can see we have a
chlorine, a bromine, an OH.

00:11:34.805 --> 00:11:37.454
So we have four different things
on each of these molecules.

00:11:37.905 --> 00:11:42.494
So what that tells you is that we
