We have the hydrogens face each
other, and then I also have both

00:12:51.385 --> 00:12:53.455
of the chlorines in the same spot.

00:12:53.905 --> 00:12:57.224
And really what you can see is
that, hey, both of these, all these

00:12:57.225 --> 00:12:59.035
different species are on the same side.

00:12:59.345 --> 00:13:03.434
And it's like you have the little
OHs waving at each other, like the

00:13:03.434 --> 00:13:05.925
reflection that I showed earlier, right?

00:13:05.925 --> 00:13:08.425
So both of these are
