00:16:08.204 --> 00:16:11.685
Let's take a look at diastereomers
and how we can determine

00:16:11.704 --> 00:16:12.964
these types of structures.

00:16:13.385 --> 00:16:16.365
Diastereomers are something that's
very, very different and can be

00:16:16.365 --> 00:16:21.225
a big struggle for introductory
organic and biochemistry students.

00:16:22.465 --> 00:16:26.025
In order for a diastereomer to
be possible, you have to have

00:16:26.025 --> 00:16:28.355
at least two chiral carbons.

00:16:28.935 --> 00:16:33.425
They cannot be mirrors of each
other and they cannot overlap,

00:16:33.595 --> 00:16:35.915
meaning they are not superimposable.

00:16:36.475 --> 00:16:41.334
These are things that are commonly seen in
biochemistry, especially revolving around

00:16:41.494 --> 00:16:46.854
Fischer projections, commonly found in
the carbohydrate family in biochemistry.

00:16:47.475 --> 00:16:51.245
So, if I have the following structure
