00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:31.390
So let's say if I label these structure 1
structure 2 structure 3 So the way to do

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:37.890
this is that 1 and 2 are enantiomers of
one another now What are diastereomers?

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:45.655
Well 1 and 3 are diastereomers Right.

00:18:46.235 --> 00:18:51.185
And one, or sorry, and two
and three are diastereomers.

00:18:52.004 --> 00:18:56.114
So what that means is that all of
the structures are diastereomers

00:18:56.144 --> 00:18:57.804
in reference to number three.

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:02.160
But they have different kind of
meanings or connotations behind

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:04.330
what kind of diastereomer.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:06.660
And this has to do with carbon numbering.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:13.439
So, for example, if I number this
like carbons so starting at the most

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.920
oxidized on top, which, what changes?

00:19:17.539 --> 00:19:24.450
Well, if I compare number 3 and
